Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

I'm constructing a Shiny app using leaflet that offers a variety of control to the user in terms of what cuts of data they want plotted and how it is plotted.

To that end, I have created a observe event which uses a series of if + else if statements to plot the proper map, depending on user input. See below (truncated example)

 observe({

    ### Storing Datasets
    dataset<- zerg()
    ucdata<- toss()

    ### Color Palettes for Map

    # colorData <- ifelse(dataset$both == "1", "both", "first_only")
    #pal <- colorFactor(c("Red", "Green"), colorData)
    pal <- colorNumeric(
      palette = "YlGnBu",
      domain = income_census$percent
    )

    ### Configure Popups
    popupEVH <- paste0("Member ID: ", dataset$member_id, "<br>", "Attributed Physician: ", dataset$docID)
    popupUC <-  paste0("Member ID: ", ucdata$member_id, "<br>", "Attributed Physician: ", ucdata$docID)

    ### Plotting the Map
    proxy <- leafletProxy("map")

    if (input$view==TRUE & input$crit=="EVH" & input$doc==FALSE && input$census==FALSE) {
      proxy %>%
        clearMarkers() %>% clearShapes() %>% clearPopups %>% clearControls %>%
        store

    }
    else if(input$view==TRUE && input$crit=="EVH" && input$doc==TRUE && input$census==FALSE) {
      proxy %>%
        clearMarkers() %>% clearShapes() %>% clearControls %>%
        addCircleMarkers(~longitude, ~latitude, layerId=~member_id,
                                            stroke=FALSE, fillOpacity=0.9, fillColor="Red", data=dataset, popup=popupEVH) %>%
        addCircleMarkers(~longitude, ~latitude, layerId=~docID, fillColor="Green", stroke=FALSE, data=docdata)
    }
    else if(input$view==TRUE && input$crit=="EVH" && input$doc==TRUE && input$census==TRUE) {
      proxy %>%
        clearMarkers() %>% clearShapes() %>% clearControls %>%
        addPolygons(data = income_census,
                fillColor = ~pal(percent),
                color = "#b2aeae", # you need to use hex colors
                fillOpacity = 0.4,
                weight = 1,
                smoothFactor = 0.2) %>%
        addLegend(pal = pal,
                values = income_census$percent,
                position = "bottomleft",
                title = "Percent of Households<br>w/ under $50k income",
                labFormat = labelFormat(suffix = "%")) %>%
        addCircleMarkers(~longitude, ~latitude, layerId=~member_id,
                         stroke=FALSE, fillOpacity=0.9, fillColor="Red", data=dataset, popup=popupEVH) %>%
        addCircleMarkers(~longitude, ~latitude, layerId=~docID, fillColor="Green", stroke=FALSE, data=docdata)

The problem with using the if + else if + else if... is that I am repeating sections of code (such as the AddCircleMarkers in Red, above)... Is there a way for me to store these layers ONCE, and then construct my conditional tree in a much more readable way?

For example, I get errors when I try to do something like this:

 observe({

    store<-addCircleMarkers(~longitude, ~latitude, layerId=~member_id,

                     stroke=FALSE, fillOpacity=0.9, fillColor="Red", data=dataset, popup=popupEVH)

    ### Plotting the Map
    proxy <- leafletProxy("map")

    if (input$view==TRUE & input$crit=="EVH" & input$doc==FALSE && input$census==FALSE) {
      proxy %>%
        clearMarkers() %>% clearShapes() %>% clearPopups %>% clearControls %>%
        store
    }

I get errors when R reaches the point where I'm trying to save that layer to the 'store' variable.

Any tips?

