I used conditionalPanel() in my script. It didn't work, but it didn't give an error neither; meaning that the plot was just displayed regardless of the condition.
That's why I kept it in the R script, but apparently this function (and the fact that there was probably sth wrong with it) did cause an error when translated to JavaScript.
Removing it solved the problem.

